index 3bbabf62..515d3825 100644
--- a/docs/BUILDING.md
+++ b/docs/BUILDING.md
@@ -284,6 +284,13 @@ NVIDIA's L4T driver (Vulkan 1.2, Tegra X1).
 | `PS3RECOMP_RSX_ENGINE=dispatch\|vtable` | Pick the draw path explicitly -- the engine's own switch, shared with Metal |
 | `RSX_ENGINE_COHERENCE_LOG=<n>` | Log the first *n* syncs between guest memory and the engine's surfaces around NV3089 transfers, with how many non-zero pixels moved |
 | `RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP=<dir>` | Capture draws pass by pass into an existing *dir*: each pass's colour targets as PPM, its zeta as PGM, and one line per pass in `passes.txt` (targets, depth range, clears, the first draw's state and textures). Starts after `RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP_AFTER=<sec>` or on the frame after one of `RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP_MINDRAWS=<n>` guest draws, and stops after `RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP_MAX=<n>` passes (default 64). `RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP_DRAWS=1` adds one line per draw to `draws.txt`. Every pass stalls the GPU for its readbacks |
+| `RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP_TRIGGER=<file>` | With `RSX_ENGINE_PASS_DUMP`: start the capture once *file* exists (checked at most once a second) instead of by time or draw count, for a scene reached by hand. When the capture ends the file is removed, and creating it again starts a new capture over the same files |
+| `PS3RECOMP_ENG_SMALL_WRITEBACK=<pixels>` | Colour targets of at most this many pixels (default 1024) that were rendered in the frame are stored to guest memory at each present, for titles that read a reduction target with the CPU; 0 turns it off |
+| `PS3RECOMP_ENG_CORNER=0` | A linear texture smaller than the colour target it points into, at the target's pitch, samples the whole target instead of a copy of its top-left corner (`eng_surface_corner`). The corner copy is what dynamic-resolution titles need; this switch is for A/B tests |
+| `PS3RECOMP_ENG_REINTERPRET=0` | Turn off the GPU reinterpretations, so these reads go through guest memory again (a readback and a CPU decode): an A8R8G8B8 colour target sampled as Y16_X16_FLOAT, and (on a backend without `depth_as_color`) a Z24S8 depth target sampled as A8R8G8B8 |
+| `PS3RECOMP_SPIRV_CACHE=<dir>` | Keep the Vulkan backend's HLSL -> SPIR-V translations on disk in an existing *dir*, one file per shader keyed by stage and the whole HLSL text and checked against the glslang version and the translator's build, so a later run loads them instead of running glslang (20-150 ms each, on the FIFO thread). A port may set a default |
+| `PS3RECOMP_SPIRV_LOG=1` | One line per shader that was not already in memory: stage, whether it came from disk or glslang, what it cost, the running counts and a steady-clock time stamp in microseconds |
+| `RSX_ENGINE_DROP_LOG=1` | Every 300 frames, print how many draw groups reached the engine, how many it drew, and how many it dropped at each early exit of `sink_end` (numbered `#n` in source order) |
 | `RSX_ENGINE_SHADER_DUMP=<dir>` | Write each new pipeline's translated programs to an existing *dir* as `pipe<handle>.vs.hlsl` and `.ps.hlsl`, the handles `passes.txt` names |
 
 Without a GPU, Mesa's lavapipe runs every check, e.g.
